    <briefdescription>
<para>Initialise a driver, run its loops and command motion. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><bold>Execution model.</bold> One driver instance (<computeroutput>struct sstep</computeroutput>) controls one motor. The application calls two functions periodically:</para>
<para><table rows="3" cols="4"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Function   </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Rate   </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Context   </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Work    </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><ref refid="group__sstep__api_1ga8c3b6798f83c32337a21d4ccdd61239b" kindref="member">sstep_fast_loop()</ref>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>fast_loop_hz</computeroutput> (PWM rate or an integer fraction of it)   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>PWM / ADC interrupt   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>current control, voltage limit, topology mapping, PWM write    </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><ref refid="group__sstep__api_1gab80d582d293872a78abc1a1a35e8e8ef" kindref="member">sstep_slow_loop()</ref>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>slow_loop_hz</computeroutput> (typically 1 kHz)   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>main loop or a timer task   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>trajectory, microstep angle, hold current, fault handling   </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>All other functions are called from the same context as <ref refid="group__sstep__api_1gab80d582d293872a78abc1a1a35e8e8ef" kindref="member">sstep_slow_loop()</ref>. The library never reads a clock, never blocks, allocates no memory and has no global state: time is given by the configured loop rates.</para>
<para><bold>Hardware access</bold> is done only through the callbacks in <ref refid="structsstep__callbacks" kindref="compound">sstep_callbacks</ref>, given once to <ref refid="group__sstep__api_1ga860a37e9ab847bb02f4102e98ea92e1c" kindref="member">sstep_init()</ref>. Measurements are passed to <ref refid="group__sstep__api_1ga8c3b6798f83c32337a21d4ccdd61239b" kindref="member">sstep_fast_loop()</ref> as raw ADC counts. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
  </compounddef>
